            0.835
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13. Throughout history, many designs of perpetual machines (using wheels, weights or magnets) have been proposed but none actually work."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.576,
            0.797,
            0.735,
            0.828
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 7.35: Opening the lid by using a spoon"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.834,
            0.742,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Why do all real machines eventually slow down and stop? Explain in terms of work and energy."
            }
          ]
        },
